# Build context for Dockerfile.backend (context is the project root, so a bare
# `COPY . .` would otherwise pull in everything below).
#
# The first block is the one that matters: without it the real .env — OIDC
# client secret, Gmail app password, SESSION_SECRET — is baked into the image
# layer, where it survives `docker history` and anything the image is later
# pushed to. Config reaches the container through compose `environment:`, never
# through a copied file.

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# ── Git history ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Large, and carries the revoked-but-still-present app password from the 13
# commits at Analyzer.py:59. No reason for it to be in a runtime image.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ── Runtime data (bind-mounted/volume-mounted at /app/backend/data) ───────────
backend/data

# ── Frontend (built by its own image, not needed by the backend) ──────────────
frontend

# ── Python cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.venv
venv
env
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache

# ── Local noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
graphify-out
*.log
nas-data
docs
*.md
!requirements.txt
